    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "One goat needs two-fifths of a hectare if it is to produce high-quality milk. How many hectares are needed for a herd of 72 goats?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$28\\frac{4}{5}$ ha",
      "worked": "One goat needs $\\frac{2}{5}$ ha. Therefore, the area needed for 72 goats is\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Area}&=72\\times\\frac{2}{5}\\text{ ha}\\\\\\text{Area}&=\\frac{144}{5}\\text{ ha}\\\\\\text{Area}&=28\\frac{4}{5}\\text{ ha}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
